213
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:17,100
Scouting gives young people the

214
00:09:17,100 --> 00:09:19,100
opportunity to develop into contributing,

215
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:22,200
capable and empathetic adults.

216
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:24,400
Scouting is much more than just

217
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:26,800
leadership, development and leadership.

218
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:28,800
You know, we all agree it's an important

219
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:30,900
quality, but it's not all there is. real

220
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:33,000
leadership actually is based on

221
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,300
a strong character.

222
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:37,200
So our principal name is developing

223
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:40,000
character, not necessarily developing

224
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:40,500
leadership.

225
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:42,600
We're not really aimed at that.

226
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:46,100
Principally, what we do is we give

227
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:47,500
people the opportunity to develop

228
00:09:47,500 --> 00:09:50,200
strong character, and the most

229
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:52,800
important things a Scout learns are

230
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:55,500
those intangible things that they

231
00:09:55,500 --> 00:09:58,700
get out of their experiences in scouting.

232
00:09:58,700 --> 00:10:01,400
I've seen touching demonstrations of

233
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:04,100
tolerance and friendship and heroic

234
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:06,200
endurance of difficult circumstances

235
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:09,300
as we watch this development of

236
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:11,600
inner character, of inner strength

237
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:14,200
in our Scouts. and without that

238
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:16,100
inner strength and that character,

239
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:18,300
there's no basis for developing

240
00:10:18,300 --> 00:10:19,200
leadership, is there?

241
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:21,300
So, just to differentiate a little

242
00:10:21,300 --> 00:10:23,700
bit between the two: develop character

243
00:10:23,700 --> 00:10:25,300
and you'll develop leadership.

244
00:10:25,900 --> 00:10:27,600
Develop just leadership.

245
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:30,800
You can do that without really touching

246
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:32,400
on those intangible character

247
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:33,600
elements sometimes.

248
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:36,400
So how do we really get at this?

249
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:39,400
How do we really get at this development

250
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:40,100
of character?

251
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:43,200
Well, one of the key elements is

252
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:45,800
something that is almost wholly unique

253
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:48,400
to scouting, and I call it real

254
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:52,700
responsibility, and we enable Scouts

255
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:55,400
to have real responsibility for

256
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:57,600
themselves and for their fellow Scouts.

257
00:10:57,600 --> 00:11:00,300
Now, what is real responsibility?

258
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:01,800
Well, I would argue that real

259
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:03,500
responsibility is the kind of

260
00:11:03,500 --> 00:11:06,100
responsibility that functions without

261
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:07,900
a safety net in a lot of ways,

262
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:10,800
You know, naturally, we're going to make

263
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:12,500
sure that our Scouts are physically

264
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:14,900
and emotionally and mentally safe-

265
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:16,300
All right, we're going to make

266
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:17,900
sure that that happens, but we're

267
00:11:17,900 --> 00:11:21,100
not going to prevent every single failure.

268
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:23,100
Scouting does its best to

269
00:11:23,100 --> 00:11:25,600
optimize the ability to succeed,

270
00:11:25,800 --> 00:11:27,800
but to have real responsibility,

271
00:11:28,300 --> 00:11:31,600
that means there's the latitude for failure.

272
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:33,400
There's little sense of accomplishment

273
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:34,900
when something is achieved in an

274
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:37,100
environment that has eliminated

275
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:39,100
all possibility of failing.

276
00:11:39,500 --> 00:11:41,500
Failures are pretty charged word,

277
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:41,800
isn't it?

278
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:44,000
We've been conditioned to think

279
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,200
that failure is altogether negative,

280
00:11:46,500 --> 00:11:49,400
but mistakes teach us some of life's

281
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:51,300
most valuable lessons.

282
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:54,100
You and I, we did not end up

283
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:56,400
where we are because we never failed.

284
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:59,100
We ended up where we are because

285
00:11:59,100 --> 00:12:02,100
we failed and learned from those failures.

286
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:05,000
As a wrestling coach, I welcomed

287
00:12:05,199 --> 00:12:08,400
the hard matches and even welcomed

288
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:11,000
losing them, because those-

289
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,900
quote- failures, unquote- provided

290
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:15,800
us with more opportunity for

291
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:18,100
learning and sharpening our skills

292
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:20,200
than just going into a match

293
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:22,100
and running over the other team.

294
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:25,200
No championship team gets to

295
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:27,800
their goal without significant development

296
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,900
and much of that development is based

297
00:12:29,900 --> 00:12:32,200
on how they incorporate the lessons

298
00:12:32,500 --> 00:12:35,000
that their failures and losses teach.

299
00:12:36,600 --> 00:12:38,700
Handled properly, failure is

300
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:42,300
a very positive influence and it

301
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:44,900
provides really sharp insight into

302
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:47,800
what you're doing and intense motivation.

303
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:49,700
So when a scout fails,

304
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:52,400
it's up to us adults to take

305
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:54,800
that failure and to turn it into a teachable

306
00:12:54,800 --> 00:12:57,500
moment and ultimately, a positive experience.

307
00:12:57,500 --> 00:12:59,500
And it's not really that hard to do, is it?

308
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:03,100
Scouting is not designed for efficiency.

309
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:04,700
There are supposed to be lots of bumps

310
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:05,900
and setbacks along the way.

311
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:07,800
They are supposed to be challenges,

312
00:13:08,100 --> 00:13:10,000
and those challenges and bumps

313
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,300
and setbacks are evidence that

314
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:16,300
scouts have real responsibility.

315
00:13:16,800 --> 00:13:19,700
We're on hand to coach and to train and encourage,

316
00:13:19,900 --> 00:13:21,800
but never to totally eliminate

317
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:23,700
the possibility of failing or

318
00:13:23,700 --> 00:13:25,900
to bail scouts out of tough spots.

319
00:13:26,300 --> 00:13:28,600
We want to work with them

320
00:13:28,900 --> 00:13:30,500
to get through these things.

321
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:32,600
So the frustrations of an

322
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:34,100
inefficient youth led program-

323
00:13:35,100 --> 00:13:37,700
They are a welcome thing to us.

324
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:39,100
We don't want to eliminate

325
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:39,600
those things,

326
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:40,800
We want to welcome them.

327
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:42,900
These experiences are the ones

328
00:13:42,900 --> 00:13:45,000
that build character

329
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:47,900
And when we take them and we accept them

330
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:49,600
as a positive influence,

331
00:13:49,700 --> 00:13:52,200
not only in our scouts lives,

332
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:53,900
but in our lives as well.

333
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:55,900
we're going to come out on top

334
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:57,500
and we're going to have

335
00:13:57,500 --> 00:14:00,700
what I like to call real responsibility

336
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,800
that leads to the development of

337
00:14:02,900 --> 00:14:04,300
good, strong character

338
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:06,300
and, as a result,

339
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:07,700
the development of leadership.

340
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,500
I'm

341
00:14:11,700 --> 00:14:12,500
down the river,

342
