00:23:46,100 --> 00:23:48,100
some challenges and difficulties

619
00:23:48,100 --> 00:23:50,100
with your fellow adults

620
00:23:50,100 --> 00:23:52,100
and with the parents of the scouts.

621
00:23:52,100 --> 00:23:54,100
you're going to learn to work with those.

622
00:23:54,100 --> 00:23:56,100
You need to make sure the committee understands

623
00:23:56,100 --> 00:23:58,100
you have a clear expectation

624
00:23:58,100 --> 00:24:00,100
that they're going to back you up,

625
00:24:00,100 --> 00:24:02,100
that they're going to intervene when parents

626
00:24:02,100 --> 00:24:04,100
or other adults become a problem

627
00:24:04,100 --> 00:24:06,100
and leave you to focus on your work

628
00:24:06,100 --> 00:24:08,100
with the scouts. You have to be

629
00:24:08,100 --> 00:24:10,100
very direct and definite about this.

630
00:24:10,100 --> 00:24:12,100
It's not something that we can just

631
00:24:12,100 --> 00:24:14,100
kind of say is understood

632
00:24:14,100 --> 00:24:16,100
without discussing it. You have to demand

633
00:24:16,100 --> 00:24:18,100
this kind of support.

634
